.nh
.TH "PB-TEAM-GET" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-get - Show one team and its current generation


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team get <team> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Show one team: its owner, current generation, state (active, suspended or deleted), the
members and resource grants, the machines shared with or owned by the team, and the team's ENV
status. Every change to the team needs the generation printed here.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for get

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb team get acme
  pb team get acme --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team(1)\fP
